==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|lang=enm|trecherie}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|lang=fro|tricherie}}, {{term|lang=fro|trecherie}}, from {{term|lang=fro|tricher}}, {{term|lang=fro|trichier||to cheat}}, from {{etyl|dum|en}} {{term|trek||a trick|lang=dum}}, from {{term|trekken||to draw, play a trick on|lang=dum}}. More at [[trick]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|treacheries}}

# Deliberate, often [[calculated]], disregard for [[trust]] or [[faith]].
# The act of violating the [[confidence]] of another, usually for personal gain.
# [[treason|Treason]].

